    {
      "id": "qvxhbg1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Matter"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Matter is defined as anything that possesses mass and occupies space.",
        "The five physical states of matter are Solid, Liquid, Gas, Plasma, and Bose-Einstein Condensate (BEC).",
        "Density is the ratio of mass to volume (Density = Mass / Volume).",
        "Elasticity is the property of a body to regain its original shape and size after removal of deforming forces.",
        "Pressure is defined as the force acting perpendicularly per unit surface area (Pressure = Force / Area)."
      ],
      "id": "cwfqz8y"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gm68cm8",
      "content": "• Matter is anything that has mass and occupies space."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xewryg5",
      "content": "• It is made up of tiny particles called atoms and molecules."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mnu46do",
      "content": "• Matter exists in different forms in nature."
    },
    {
      "id": "t07gull",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. States of Matter"
    },
    {
      "id": "jmq67zi",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>State</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Properties</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Solid</p>",
            "<p>Fixed shape and volume</p>",
            "<p>Iron, wood, ice</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Liquid</p>",
            "<p>Fixed volume but no fixed shape</p>",
            "<p>Water, oil, milk</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Gas</p>",
            "<p>No fixed shape or volume</p>",
            "<p>Air, oxygen, carbon dioxide</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6sxg40v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Physical Properties of Matter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ml5z8z4",
      "content": "• Mass – amount of matter in a substance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vfcldzg",
      "content": "• Volume – space occupied by matter."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Matter is anything that has mass and occupies space, existing in various states depending on thermal energy and intermolecular forces.",
      "id": "68yxltb"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5d8dq2i",
      "content": "• Density – mass per unit volume."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uybyvp7",
      "content": "• Elasticity – ability of a material to regain its original shape."
    },
    {
      "id": "huq06t9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Changes in States of Matter"
    },
    {
      "id": "cxs7g4t",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Process</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Melting</p>",
            "<p>Solid changes into liquid</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Freezing</p>",
            "<p>Liquid changes into solid</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Evaporation</p>",
            "<p>Liquid changes into gas</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Condensation</p>",
            "<p>Gas changes into liquid</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sublimation</p>",
            "<p>Solid changes directly into gas</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
