    },
    {
      "id": "1ztxw15",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Elasticity"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sogoa21",
      "content": "Elasticity is the property of a material to regain its original shape after deformation when the external force is removed."
    },
    {
      "id": "ku05ke9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Pressure"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "typ8ocq",
      "content": "Pressure is defined as force acting per unit area."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yohchgd",
      "content": "Formula: Pressure = Force / Area"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "5szp3i6",
      "content": "SI Unit = Pascal (Pa)"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Sublimation is the direct conversion of a solid into a gas without passing through the liquid phase (e.g., Camphor, Naphthalene, Dry Ice).",
        "Atmospheric pressure decreases with altitude, which lowers the boiling point of liquids at higher elevations.",
        "Hooke's Law states that within the elastic limit, stress is directly proportional to strain.",
        "Bose-Einstein Condensate is formed by cooling a gas of extremely low density to super low temperatures near absolute zero."
      ],
      "id": "ehs8mj5"
    },
    {
